ship labels.                   \u2502\n\u2502     - NEVER diagram Terraform file names (`main.tf`, `variables.tf`,         \u2502\n\u2502  `outputs.tf`) or directory trees in the Mermaid diagram.                    \u2502\n\u2502  4. The first line of your response must be: PROJECT_SLUG: <slug>            \u2502\n\u2502     - The slug MUST be a descriptive kebab-case name derived from the        \u2502\n\u2502  requirement.                                                                \u2502\n\u2502     - NEVER use generic names like \"terraform-project\" or timestamps.        \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  EKS-SPECIFIC RULES:                                                         \u2502\n\u2502  - If creating EKS, ALWAYS include at least 2 public subnets in 2 different  \u2502\n\u2502  AZs (EKS requires this).                                                    \u2502\n\u2502  - ALWAYS include IAM policy attachments (AmazonEKSClusterPolicy,            \u2502\n\u2502  AmazonEKSWorkerNodePolicy, AmazonEC2ContainerRegistryReadOnly,              \u2502\n\u2502  AmazonEKS_CNI_Policy).                                                      \u2502\n\u2502  - ALWAYS include security groups for the cluster and nodes.                 \u2502\n\u2502  - The design MUST include a `provider` block and `terraform {               \u2502\n\u2502  required_providers { } }` block.                                            \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2570\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u256f\n\n\u001b[35m[Finalize] todos_count=0, todos_with_results=0\u001b[0m\n\u256d\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500 \u2705 Agent Final Answer \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u256e\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  Agent: Universal Cloud Architect                                            \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  Final Answer:                                                               \u2502\n\u2502  PROJECT_SLUG: aws-s3-vault-storage                                          \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  ### 1. Provider and Resource Identification                                 \u2502\n\u2502  *   **Provider:** `hashicorp/aws`                                           \u2502\n\u2502  *   **Resources:**                                                          \u2502\n\u2502      *   `aws_s3_bucket`: For storage.                                       \u2502\n\u2502      *   `aws_s3_bucket_versioning`: To enable versioning.                   \u2502\n\u2502      *   `aws_s3_bucket_lifecycle_configuration`: To define the 30-day       \u2502\n\u2502  Glacier transition.                                                         \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  ### 2. Modular Folder Layout                                                \u2502\n\u2502  ```text                                                                     \u2502\n\u2502  .                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502  \u251c\u2500\u2500 main.tf                 # Root module calling submodules                \u2502\n\u2502  \u251c\u2500\u2500 providers.tf            # Provider configuration                        \u2502\n\u2502  \u251c\u2500\u2500 modules/                                                                \u2502\n\u2502  \u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 storage/                                                            \u2502\n\u2502  \u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 main.tf         # S3 bucket, versioning, and lifecycle          \u2502\n\u2502  resources                                                                   \u2502\n\u2502  \u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 variables.tf                                                    \u2502\n\u2502  \u2502       \u2514\u2500\u2500 outputs.tf                                                      \u2502\n\u2502  ```                                                                         \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  ### 3. Infrastructure Code                                                  \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  **providers.tf**                                                            \u2502\n\u2502  ```hcl                                                                      \u2502\n\u2502  terraform {                                                                 \u2502\n\u2502    required_providers {                                                      \u2502\n\u2502      aws = {                                                                 \u2502\n\u2502        source  = \"hashicorp/aws\"                                             \u2502\n\u2502        version = \"~> 5.0\"